      "message": "As written, the output of `afind` includes .repo, .git, and out directories.\n\nIf the default is changed to `args\u003d( -print )`, then those are excluded.\n\nAlso, in my workspace, I see this, which may not be quite what we want either:\n```\n% afind . -name \u0027.*\u0027 | head -8\n.\n./out\n./frameworks/proto_logging/.git\n./frameworks/proto_logging/stats/express/.clang-format\n./frameworks/proto_logging/stats/.gitignore\n./frameworks/proto_logging/stats/stats_log_api_gen/.clang-format\n./frameworks/hardware/interfaces/.clang-format\n./frameworks/hardware/interfaces/.git\n```\n\nIf I use `afind . -name \u0027.*\u0027 -print`, then the .git directories (et. al.) go away.",
